{"type":"WebSearch","query":"California Proposition 37 2026 site:lwvc.org ballot recommendation","content":"The League of Women Voters of California (LWVC) recommends **NO** on California Proposition 37 (2026), titled "Loan Program for Middle-Income Buyers of New Homes."[[1]](https://lwvc.org/ballot-recommendations-nov-3-2026/)

This is for the November 3, 2026 general election. The LWVC's position is based on their analysis that while the measure addresses down-payment barriers, it could add unaffordable monthly costs via a second mortgage, fail to target those facing the greatest housing barriers (including racial and economic inequities), lack ties to good planning, and leave too many key details (like interest rates and terms) undecided. They note it does not meet the test for effective homeownership programs that lower total costs and support communities.[[2]](https://lwvc.org/ballot-recommendations/)

For the full analysis, visit the LWVC's Ballot Recommendations page.","citations":["https://lwvc.org/ballot-recommendations-nov-3-2026/","https://lwvc.org/ballot-recommendations/"],"allowed_domains":null}
